; a beauty which I do not recollect has struck any painter.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["marbleize"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["all the marbles","Blue Marble","blue marble tree","Carrara marble","emmarble","enmarble","fire marble","green marble","lose one's marbles","Luna marble","marbelic","Marble Arch","Marble Bar","marble beef","marble berry","marble cake","Marble Canyon","marble cheese","marble cichlid","marble egg","marblefish","marble fox","marble goby","marble-hearted","Marble Hill","marbleization","marbleless","marblelike","marbleness","marble orchard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marble#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f8d6a9835c738835c5","definition":"To get or have the streaked or swirled appearance of certain types of marble, for example due to the incomplete mixing of viscous ingredients, or the uneven application of paint or other colorants.","example":"Scent the entire batch and then color half with the blue colorant. Pour both parts back into your soap pot. Do not stir. Pour in a circular motion into a block mold. The pouring action will cause the soap to marble.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["all the marbles","Blue Marble","blue marble tree","Carrara marble","emmarble","enmarble","fire marble","green marble","lose one's marbles","Luna marble","marbelic","Marble Arch","Marble Bar","marble beef","marble berry","marble cake","Marble Canyon","marble cheese","marble cichlid","marble egg","marblefish","marble fox","marble goby","marble-hearted","Marble Hill","marbleization","marbleless","marblelike","marbleness","marble orchard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marble#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1b0575802b74e9f02c","definition":"To cause meat, usually beef, pork, or lamb, to be interlaced with fat so that its appearance resembles that of marble.","example":"Their flesh is soft (tender), and they throw a portion of their fat among the lean so as to marble it. The beef is of a better quality and they take on fat much easier.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["marbleize"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["all the marbles","Blue Marble","blue marble tree","Carrara marble","emmarble","enmarble","fire marble","green marble","lose one's marbles","Luna marble","marbelic","Marble Arch","Marble Bar","marble beef","marble berry","marble cake","Marble Canyon","marble cheese","marble cichlid","marble egg","marblefish","marble fox","marble goby","marble-hearted","Marble Hill","marbleization","marbleless","marblelike","marbleness","marble orchard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marble#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:044810b5571f166036","definition":"To become interlaced with fat; (of fat) to interlace through meat.","example":"We've gone mostly to black bulls — Angus bulls because today the packers like black cattle. They seem to marble better.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["all the marbles","Blue Marble","blue marble tree","Carrara marble","emmarble","enmarble","fire marble","green marble","lose one's marbles","Luna marble","marbelic","Marble Arch","Marble Bar","marble beef","marble berry","marble cake","Marble Canyon","marble cheese","marble cichlid","marble egg","marblefish","marble fox","marble goby","marble-hearted","Marble Hill","marbleization","marbleless","marblelike","marbleness","marble orchard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"ht